{
  "id": "Compound::DB00667 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Histamine Phosphate is shown to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, specifically Cyp2c9, Cyp2d6, and Cyp3a4, through a series of mechanistic pathways. The binding of Histamine Phosphate to Cyp2c9 and Cyp2d6 is supported by direct interaction evidence, which in turn leads to their participation in metabolic activities. These activities involve oxidoreductase and aromatase functions, which are critical for the metabolism of various substrates. The involvement of Cyp3a4 in these pathways suggests a potential role in the metabolic processing of compounds that are substrates of these CYP enzymes. The integrated evidence indicates that Histamine Phosphate may influence Cyp3a4 through its interaction with other CYP enzymes, potentially modulating their activity in the context of metabolic pathways. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct impact of Histamine Phosphate on Cyp3a4.",
